'''Vines''' are climbable non-solid vegetation blocks that grow on walls.

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Vines can be destroyed with any item, but using [[shears]] is the only way to collect them. Shears enchanted with [[Efficiency]] are more efficient when used on vines; Efficiency II and above allows vines to be [[instant mining|instantly broken]].<ref>{{ytl|bhkx7mosH7g|t=444}}</ref> Using an axe on vines can also increase efficiency, but does not allow for collection, even with [[Silk Touch]]. If multiple vines exist within the same block space, breaking one of them breaks all of them instead of just the one targeted<ref>{{bug|MC-129114|||Invalid}}</ref> and results in only a single vine dropping<ref>{{bug|MC-123140||Vines lost when shearing many at once in a single block space|Unresolved}}</ref>. Shears used by a dispenser cannot break vines.
{{breaking row|horizontal=1|Vines|Axe|drop=0|shears=1|sword=0}}

=== Natural generation ===
{{main|Vines (feature)}}
Vines are naturally generated in [[jungle]]s, [[swamp]]s, [[mangrove swamp]]s and [[lush caves]]. [[Jungle tree]]s of both sizes have vines on their trunks and canopy edges, and vines grow on the sides of jungle terrain. Vines are also naturally generated on [[oak]] trees in swamps and [[mangrove]] trees. {{IN|bedrock}}, vines can also generate on [[dying tree|dying]] oak, [[spruce]], jungle and [[dark oak]] trees.

Vines can generate growing on the stumps of oak and jungle [[fallen tree]]s.

Vines are found in [[jungle pyramid]]s, [[abandoned camp]]s and the allium room in [[woodland mansion]]s. They can also generate on the watchtower walls of [[pillager outpost]]s.

Vines can also be found in the {{cd|display_2}} structure in the [[trial chambers]].

{{block distribution}}

=== Trading ===
[[Wandering trader]]s may sell 3 vines for 1 [[emerald]].
{{Trade sources}}

=== Mob loot ===
{{IN|bedrock}}, [[wandering traders]] have a chance of 25% (increased by 1% per level of [[Looting]]) to drop 3 vines when killed while showing the item as trade offer, if the player holds an [[emerald]].

=== Post-generation ===
Vines generate on 2×2 jungle trees grown from [[sapling]]s, or mangrove trees grown from [[propagule]]s.

{{IN|bedrock}}, vines generate on [[dying tree]]s, which can sometimes be grown from saplings.

== Behavior ==
On each [[random tick]], the vine block has a 25% chance to spread in a randomly selected direction. Their spreading can be toggled by the {{cd|spread_vines}} [[game rule]]{{only|je}}. Vines spread to adjacent blocks under certain conditions:

* Downward:
** If the block below is air, each side (north, south, east, and west) with vines has a 50% chance to spread downward.
** If the block below is a block, each side of that block with vines on the ticked block has a 50% chance of gaining vines.

* Upward: 
** If the block above is air and there are fewer than 4 other vine blocks in a 9×9×3 area surrounding the ticked vine block, each side (north, south, east, and west) with vines has a 50% chance to spread upward if that side is backed by a block that vines can be placed on.

* Horizontally: 
** If the current vine block isn't covering the target direction and there are fewer than 4 other vine blocks in a 9×9×3 area surrounding the ticked vine block, then:
*** If the block in the target direction is air, then it tries:

