'''Warped nylium''' is a variant of [[netherrack]] that generates in [[the Nether]].

== Obtaining ==
=== Breaking ===
Nylium drops itself only when mined with a [[pickaxe]] enchanted with [[Silk Touch]]; if mined with a normal pickaxe, it drops [[netherrack]]. If mined without a pickaxe, it drops nothing.

{{breaking row|horizontal=1|Warped Nylium|drop=0|Pickaxe|Wooden}}

=== Natural generation ===
Warped nylium generates in the [[warped forest]] biome.

{{Block distribution}}

=== Mob loot ===
Warped nylium is dropped when an [[enderman]] dies while holding it.

=== Post-generation ===
{{ctrl|Using}} [[bone meal]] on [[netherrack]] that is placed next to or adjacent to warped nylium transforms the netherrack into warped nylium. [[Air]] must be above the netherrack during this process. This transformation can also be done by activating a [[dispenser]] with bone meal directly into that netherrack block.  If both types of nylium are present, there is an equal chance of either being spread.

=== Renewability ===
{{exclusive|Bedrock|section=1}}
As [[netherrack]] generates in [[Nether portal]]s spawn floating, using bone meal on netherrack turns them into warped nylium, making it [[renewable]].

== Usage ==
Similar to [[grass block]]s and [[mycelium]], warped nylium decays (based on [[random tick]]s) into netherrack when an full [[opaque]] block is placed above it. However, unlike grass blocks and mycelium, it does not decay underneath [[water]] or [[lava]].<ref>{{bug|MC-173356|||WAI}}</ref> It decays when covered with [[snow]].<ref>{{bug|MC-174639|||WAI}}</ref>

Like mycelium and [[podzol]], [[mushroom]]s can remain on warped nylium blocks in any [[light]] level. [[Huge mushroom]]s can be grown by using bone meal on mushrooms planted on warped nylium.

[[Warped fungi]] can likewise be grown into [[huge warped fungi]] using [[bone meal]]. However, bone meal cannot be applied to [[crimson fungus]] on top of the warped nylium, even if it can be positioned there, it is necessary to plant in [[crimson nylium]].

Similar to [[grass block]]s, the player can apply [[bone meal]] to warped nylium, when it has [[air]] above. The warped nylium and surrounding blocks attempt to position vegetation from the Nether, according to the table below. In all cases, the vegetation can only replace air.

